mono.vendor/patches/luau-lsp/call-hierarchy-function-name-copy.patch

Keep GCC 13 warning checks enabled when building call hierarchy support.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH
    GCC 13 reports maybe-uninitialized in the string storage of the disengaged
    optional when a temporary FunctionName is moved into the functions tuple.
    Constructing a named const FunctionName and copying it into the tuple avoids
    that move while preserving the same name and empty detail. This replaces the
    recipe's warning exemption without weakening upstream's -Wall -Werror.

WHERE IT GOES
    FindAllFunctionsVisitor::visit(Luau::AstStatLocalFunction*) in
    src/operations/CallHierarchy.cpp, at the funcs.emplace_back call.

WHEN IT STOPS APPLYING
    Re-point this hunk at the local-function tuple insertion. If upstream no
    longer moves the temporary, remove the patch after a cold GCC 13 build with
    warnings still fatal. scripts/vendor-tree.sh applies this only to the copied
    vendor tree and stops when a patch no longer applies.

VALIDATION
    just typecheck-editor rebuilds the patched language server and checks all
    authored examples. Check the cold build output for warnings as well as its
    exit status; no compiler-warning suppression is needed by this patch.

diff --git a/src/operations/CallHierarchy.cpp b/src/operations/CallHierarchy.cpp
--- a/src/operations/CallHierarchy.cpp
+++ b/src/operations/CallHierarchy.cpp
@@ -68,7 +68,8 @@ struct FindAllFunctionsVisitor : public Luau::AstVisitor
 
     bool visit(class Luau::AstStatLocalFunction* node) override
     {
-        funcs.emplace_back(FunctionName{node->name->name.value, std::nullopt}, node->location, node->name->location, node->func);
+        const FunctionName functionName{node->name->name.value, std::nullopt};
+        funcs.emplace_back(functionName, node->location, node->name->location, node->func);
         return true;
     }
 
